changes. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>46</volume>:<fpage>387</fpage>&#x02013;397.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17209549</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Anderson, A. C. <year>2005</year>. Two crystal structures of dihydrofolate reductase-thymidylate synthase from <italic>Cryptosporidium hominis</italic> reveal protein-ligand interactions including a structural basis for observed antifolate resistance. <source>Acta Crystallogr. F Struct. Biol. Cryst. Commun.</source> <volume>61</volume>:<fpage>258</fpage>&#x02013;262.</citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Elcock, A. H., M. J. Potter, D. A. Matthews, D. R. Knighton, and J. A. McCammon. <year>1996</year>. Electrostatic channeling in the bifunctional enzyme dihydrofolate reductase-thymidylate synthase. <source>J. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>262</volume>:<fpage>370</fpage>&#x02013;374.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8845002</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Elcock, A. H., and J. A. McCammon. <year>1996</year>. Evidence for electrostatic channeling in a fusion protein of malate dehydrogenase and citrate synthase. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>35</volume>:<fpage>12652</fpage>&#x02013;12658.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8841108</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Amaro, R., and Z. Luthey-Schulten. <year>2004</year>. Molecular dynamics simulations of substrate channeling through an <italic>&#x003b1;</italic>-<italic>&#x003b2;</italic> barrel protein. <source>Chem. Phys.</source> <volume>307</volume>:<fpage>147</fpage>&#x02013;155.</citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Floquet, N., S. Mouilleron, R. Daher, B. Maigret, B. Badet, and M. A. Badet-Denisot. <year>2007</year>. Ammonia channeling in bacterial glucosamine-6-phosphate synthase (GLMS): molecular dynamics simulations and kinetic studies of protein mutants. <source>FEBS Lett.</source> <volume>581</volume>:<fpage>2981</fpage>&#x02013;2987.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17559838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sun, M. H., J. L. Andreassi, S. Q. Liu, R. Pinto, J. A. Triccas, and T. S. Leyh. <year>2005</year>. The trifunctional sulfate-activating complex (SAC) of mycobacterium tuberculosis. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>280</volume>:<fpage>7861</fpage>&#x02013;7866.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15615729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Sun, M. H., and T. S. Leyh. <year>2006</year>. Channeling in sulfate activating complexes. <source>Biochemistry.</source> <volume>45</volume>:<fpage>11304</fpage>&#x02013;11311.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16981690</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><label>21.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Cheng, Y. H., J. K. Suen, Z. Radi&#x00107;, S. D. Bond, M. J. Holst, and J. A. McCammon. <year>2007</year>. Continuum simulations of acetylcholine diffusion with reaction-determined boundaries in neuromuscular junction models. <source>Biophys. Chem.</source> <volume>127</volume>:<fpage>129</fpage>&#x02013;139.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17307283</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><label>22.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Holst, M., N. Baker, and F. Wang. <year>2000</year>. Adaptive multilevel finite element solution of the Poisson-Boltzmann equation. I. Algorithms and examples. <source>J. Comput. Chem.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>1319</fpage>&#x02013;1342.</citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><label>23.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Baker, N., M. Holst, and F. Wang. <year>2000</year>. Adaptive multilevel finite element solution of the Poisson-Boltzmann equation. II. Refinement at solvent-accessible surfaces in biomolecular systems. <source>J. Comput. Chem.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>1343</fpage>&#x02013;1352.</citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><label>24.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Baker, N. A., D. Sept, S. Joseph, M. J. Holst, and J. A. McCammon. <year>2001</year>. Electrostatics of nanosystems: application to microtubules and the ribosome. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>10037</fpage>&#x02013;10041.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11517324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><label>25.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Song, Y. H., Y. J. Zhang, C. L. Bajaj, and N. A. Baker. <year>2004</year>. Continuum diffusion reaction rate calculations of wild-type and mutant mouse acetylcholinesterase: adaptive finite element analysis. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>87</volume>:<fpage>1558</fpage>&#x02013;1566.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15345536</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><label>26.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Song, Y. H., Y. J. Zhang, T. Y. Shen, C. L. Bajaj, J. A. McCammon, and N. A. Baker. <year>2004</year>. Finite element solution of the steady-state Smoluchowski equation for rate constant calculations. <source>Biophys. J.</source> <volume>86</volume>:<fpage>2017</fpage>&#x02013;2029.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15041644</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><label>27.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Yu, Z., M. Holst, Y. Cheng, and J. A. McCammon. <year>2008</year>. Feature-preserving adaptive mesh generation for molecular modeling. <source>J. Mol. Graph. Model.</source> <volume>26</volume>:<fpage>1370</fpage>&#x02013;1380.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18337134</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><label>28.</label><citation citation-type="journal">Zhang, D. Q., J. Suen, Y. J. Zhang, Y. H. Song, Z. Radi&#x00107;, P. Taylor, M. J. Holst, C. Bajaj, N. A. Baker, and J. A. McCammon. <year>2005</year>. Tetrameric mouse acetylcholinesterase: continuum diffusion rate calculations by solving the steady-state Smoluchowski equation using finite element m